If you looked into linux tablets you've probably came across this already but I'm including it 
here just in case. The linux surface project is a really cool project that aims to make Microsoft
Surface Tablets to be functional with linux. When I tried to install Fedora 42 on my surface pro 6,
it wouldn't even install, so I had to install the surface linux kernel inside the liveboot to get
it to even install in the first place but once that was done it's incredible how well it worked.
Almost everything fucntions as you expect it with the camera quality being shot, the touchscreen 
usage also works fairly well with only some ocassional misinputs. 

https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface
